BitCheck – Bitcoin Wallet Balance Checker

BitCheck is a lightweight web application that lets users check the real-time on-chain balance of any Bitcoin wallet address.  
It uses the public "Blockstream Bitcoin API" to fetch address data and displays the balance in both BTC and satoshis.

This project was built as part of my portfolio for full-stack and backend development practice.

---

Features

-  Look up any Bitcoin wallet address  
-  Shows balance in "BTC" and "satoshis"  
-  Displays total confirmed on-chain transactions  
-  Fast backend using Node.js + Express  
-  Clean and responsive UI  
-  Uses Blockstream's public blockchain API (no API key required)

---
Live Demo

https://bitcheck-wrk5.onrender.com/

Click the link above to test the deployed version instantly.

---

🛠 Tech Stack

**Backend**
- Node.js  
- Express.js  
- Axios (API requests)

**Frontend**
- HTML  
- CSS  
- Vanilla JavaScript (Fetch API)

**Infrastructure**
- Public Blockstream REST API

---
To Run the project loaclly


1. Clone the repository
```bash
git clone https://github.com/harshituppala/bitcheck.git
cd bitcheck

2. Install dependencies
npm install

3. Start the development server
npm run dev

4. visit the local app
click on the link that looks like "http://localhost:3000"

---

API Used

Blockstream Bitcoin REST API
https://blockstream.info/api/

